% refs.bib: single source of truth for publications.
% Used by: cv.tex, resume.tex, you_resume.tex (biblatex/biber), tools/pubs.py
% (generates cv/writing.tex + cv/writing_r.tex), and the website (copied to
% christopheryou.github.io/data/publications.bib by the site-sync skill).
%
% Conventions
%   author      Write my name as "You, Christopher". It is highlighted
%               automatically (see pubstyle.tex); never add markup to it.
%   year/month  Numeric. Leave year out for unpublished work and set pubstate.
%   pubstate    inpreparation | submitted | inreview | forthcoming   (omit once published)
%   keywords    Exactly one category: journal | conference | poster | mentored
%               Add "selected" to feature the paper on the website home page.
%   doi         Bare DOI (10.xxxx/...), no https://doi.org/ prefix.
%   shorttitle  Optional. Shorter title used on the one-page resume.
%   shortvenue  Optional. Short venue used on the resume and website (e.g. ACM IVA).
%   pdf         Optional. Filename in the website's samples/ folder.
%   pdfnote     Optional. Caveat shown next to the PDF link on the website.
%   Protect proper nouns and acronyms in titles with braces: {AI}, {ALEX}.
% =============================================================================

